Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO):
By opening a pull request to this repository, you certify under the Developer
Certificate of Origin (https://developercertificate.org/) that you wrote or
have the right to submit the contribution under CC-BY-4.0, and every commit
must carry a `Signed-off-by: Name <email>` trailer (`git commit -s`).

Note on per-artifact `license` fields:
Per-artifact `license` fields are FORBIDDEN on lessons, overlays, aliases, and
concepts (they inherit this repo-level CC-BY-4.0 license). Only `kind: asset`
artifacts (such as 3D glTF models or synthetic audio metadata) may declare a
third-party `license`.
